{title: The old gospel ship}
{subtitle: Hymnal 367}
{x_theme: praise, heaven, joy, prayer}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/The old gospel ship.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
O I’m gonna take a trip, in the good old gospel ship
I’m going far beyond the sky
O I’m gonna shout and sing until the heavens ring
When I’m bidding this world goodbye

{comment: Verse 1}
I have good news to bring and that is why I sing
All my joys with you I’ll share
I’m going to take a trip in the old gospel ship
And go sailing thru the air

{comment: Verse 2}
O I can scarcely wait, I know I’ll not be late
For I’ll spend my time in  prayer
And when my ship comes in I will leave this world of sin
And go sailing thu the air

{comment: Verse 3}
If you’re ashamed of me, You have no cause to be
For with Christ I am an heir
If too much fault you find, You will sure be left behind
While I go sailing thru the air
